Subject: [PATCH 2/5] mmdevapi: make event-driven exclusive-mode streams usable

Two problems on the standard low-latency path,
Initialize(EXCLUSIVE | AUDCLNT_STREAMFLAGS_EVENTCALLBACK):

  - adjust_timing() refused the combination outright with
    AUDCLNT_E_DEVICE_IN_USE on an idle device, above the driver, so changing
    audio driver could not help;
  - the buffer handed back was not usable a period at a time, so GetBuffer for
    a full period returned BUFFER_TOO_LARGE with padding stuck at the whole
    buffer.

DJ applications probe and open in exclusive mode; with these fixed, the sample
rate list populates and playback sustains.

---
--- a/dlls/mmdevapi/client.c
+++ b/dlls/mmdevapi/client.c
@@ -145,9 +145,33 @@
                 if (*duration != *period)
                     return AUDCLNT_E_BUFDURATION_PERIOD_NOT_EQUAL;
 
-                FIXME("EXCLUSIVE mode with EVENTCALLBACK\n");
-
-                return AUDCLNT_E_DEVICE_IN_USE;
+                /* RBW-MMDEV2: event-driven exclusive mode.
+                 *
+                 * The earlier version of this hunk assumed the backends ran a
+                 * multi-period ring underneath and left duration == period. They
+                 * do not: duration IS the mmdevapi buffer, so the client got a
+                 * buffer exactly one period long. get_render_buffer then refuses
+                 * every request, because
+                 *
+                 *     held_frames + frames > bufsize_frames
+                 *
+                 * is true for a full period whenever ANY frames are still held.
+                 * Measured with rekordbox 7.2.17 on a DDJ-400: held_frames
+                 * pinned at 1024 == bufsize == period, 6,963,363
+                 * GetCurrentPadding calls against 20 GetBuffer calls, and 20
+                 * stream rebuilds in 100 s as the starved stream collapsed and
+                 * was recreated.
+                 *
+                 * Give it several periods of slack, exactly as the non-event
+                 * exclusive path immediately below already does. The client is
+                 * still signalled once per period and still writes a period at a
+                 * time; it simply now has somewhere to put it. GetBufferSize
+                 * reports the real size, so a client that sizes itself from that
+                 * stays correct. */
+                if (*duration < 4 * *period)
+                    *duration = 4 * *period;
+                TRACE("RBW-MMDEV2 exclusive+event: duration widened to %lu for period %lu\n",
+                      (ULONG)*duration, (ULONG)*period);
             } else if (*duration < 8 * *period)
                 *duration = 8 * *period; /* May grow above 2s. */
         }
